Subject: Re: AlphaBIOS to SRM firmware conversion on an AlphaPC 164LX 533MHz -- Solution
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=100706931502701

On Thu, Nov 29, 2001 at 01:04:09PM -0800, Alexander Poquet wrote:
> Here's the solution, though:
> 
> >All of the parts required to convert AlphaBIOS to SRM on the LX are
> >available at http://www.freebsd.org/~msmith/alpha/pc164lx

Any firmware in http://www.freebsd.org/~msmith/alpha/ is *way* old!

Three months ago I installed SRM on a 164LX and I found it *QUITE* a
PITA.  I remember thinking thank goodness I'd never have to go thru it
again.  I guess I should have written down exactly what I did.

The flash ROM is not big enough to hold both AlphaBIOS and SRM (on
platforms where it is, it is trivial to switch between the two).  I have
a firmware CD which I could make an ISO available, but from AlphaBIOS
there is no way to boot from CDROM!

I found more useful documention in a rather tucked out of the way
directory (maybe w/in "archive") at
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/

P.S. if you want to use a Adaptec AHA-2940UW SCSI controller you need the
SRM from Dompaq's "6.0" or later firmware collection site.

