From openbsd-alpha  Thu Nov 29 21:04:09 2001
From: Alexander Poquet <atpoquet () ucdavis ! edu>
Date: Thu, 29 Nov 2001 21:04:09 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: AlphaBIOS to SRM firmware conversion on an AlphaPC 164LX 533MHz -- Solution
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=100706796627356

Hey all,

I recently posted a question regarding getting SRM firmware onto my Alpha,
which in retrospect was an extremely newbie question (well, I am trying to
learn this architecture ;p) and after a little more research was able to
find a solution.  I'm including it here in hopes that this list is indexed,
with my original post quoted below to facilitate searches.  Sorry for the
spam.

In actuality, I'm not sure what the base problem with my attack was;
obviously
what DEC was telling me to do to fix my problem wasn't the solution they'd
advertised.  Some folks on the FreeBSD-alpha newsgroup had posted a solution
that was indexed, but because the original problem wasn't quoted it didn't
show up in direct searches.  I found it anyway, felt like a moron for
posting.

Here's the solution, though:

>All of the parts required to convert AlphaBIOS to SRM on the LX are
>available at http://www.freebsd.org/~msmith/alpha/pc164lx
>
>Put all the files on a floppy, boot AlphaBIOS, select Upgrade, it boots
>AlphaBIOS again, select Upgrade, then pick SRM from the combo box and
>let it do its stuff.
>
>You may want to then upgrade to a later SRM.
>

I'm still sort of curious what sort of crack DEC was smoking ;) and actually
what the notable differences between their method and the one proposed by
the FreeBSD community.  When I figure it out I'll let you know.

How many folks are on this list, anyway?  Is there anywhere/way to check?

Alexander

On Tue, Nov 27, 2001 at 01:10:30PM -0800, Alexander Poquet wrote:
> Hello all,
>
> I recently acquired an AlphaPC 164LX 533MHz workstation which had been (god
> forbid) running Windows NT, and as such was equipped with the Windows NT
> accelerated AlphaBIOS firmware rather than the SRM firmware required to
boot
> our OS of choice.
>
> I went to http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware and followed the
> instructions for my hardware, acquiring a file called lx164_v5_8.exe.  I
> formatted a FAT floppy and renamed this file to 'fwupdate.exe' (as per the
> instructions) and chose 'Update AlphaBIOS' from the AlphaBIOS menu.
>
> It frobbed the floppy for a bit and then rebooted, and gave me this:
> (the floppy is still in the drive)
